\newlabel{_Ref222510092}{{8}{22}{Global parameter sensitivity based on the Morris method expressed as absolute mean effects (\(\mu ^*\)) for the baseline FSIM model (a) and the extended FSIM-S model incorporating the spore-pressure formulation (b). Parameters are ranked by decreasing \(\mu ^*\), representing their overall influence magnitude on model output aggregated across multiple random seeds. Parameter abbreviations: ZVPD = zoospore\_alive\_\_vpd; DIRM = dispersal\_\_rain\_min; IC = infection\_\_infection\_condition; TMSO = thresholds\_\_min\_spores; STMX = sporulation\_\_Tmax; MTWN = mp\_tmp\_\_rh\_wet\_night; DIWM = dispersal\_\_wind\_min; STOP = sporulation\_\_Topt; STMI = sporulation\_\_Tmin; ZARA = zoospore\_alive\_\_rain; DERM = deposition\_\_rain\_min; SMMI = sporulation\_\_MP\_min; ISED = incubation\_\_spl\_end; SAP = spore\_\_alpha\_pos; SAN = spore\_\_alpha\_neg. Error bars indicate variability across aggregated runs}{figure.caption.44}{}}
